commit 63b6f634c6e1e82d2ccf9d01fb04ab6e4d233b34
Author: lora-dataset-studio <noreply@lora-dataset-studio.dev>
Date:   Fri Aug 7 01:29:07 2026 +0200

    feat(captions): each caption says who wrote it, and the run says who wrote what
    
    The default captioning backend is 'auto', which is a CHAIN: JoyCaption writes what
    it can, then the Ollama vision model covers the images JoyCaption did not caption.
    Both halves land in the same column, in the same font, and nothing on screen told
    them apart — so a caption that describes something the image does not contain read
    exactly like one that reads it correctly.
    
    The data already existed. `caption_origin` has been stamped by every caption writer
    since services/caption_origin.py landed, and it was used for exactly one decision
    (which rows a forced 🔄 Re-caption spares) while the screens where a caption is READ
    still showed an anonymous string. utils/captionEngines.js named this follow-up in its
    own header; this is it.
    
    WHERE THE AUTHOR IS NOW VISIBLE
      · bank tile tooltip — the caption is prefixed by who wrote it;
      · dataset tile — a chip on the caption's own action row;
      · expanded caption editor — a line per box, long and short separately (the short
        caption has its own writers, so the long one's stamp cannot answer for it);
      · identity-leak list — where captions are read one by one to decide what to redo.
    
    WHAT THE RUN NOW REPORTS. The bank caption pass appends '— 340 by JoyCaption, 87 by
    the Ollama vision model' to its result, counted from the rows it actually STAMPED —
    not from the pool it started with (which counts rows the pass then skipped as stale,
    deleted or newer-caption-won) and not from the backend that was asked for ('auto'
    would mislabel roughly half a bank). 'asserted' is never in that list: no pass writes
    it. The dataset lane already had these counts; the bank did not.
    
    An engine name this build does not know is printed under its own name rather than
    dropped, and a write whose engine reported no name is counted apart instead of being
    attributed to one — NULL means 'never recorded', never 'machine'.
    
    Payloads gain caption_origin (bank rows, dataset images) and caption_short_origin
    (dataset images). Additive keys only; no stored value is renamed.
    
    Also lands the NSFW notice in the bank caption launch window
    (components/bank/captionNsfwNotice.js) — see the next commit's tests for its
    threshold and its evidence base.
